module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.EpiLocallySurjective
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.InvertibleLocalSummand
public import StacksFrontier.Topology.Sheaves.Functors.Module.RingedSpace
public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# A pullback of sheaves of modules is locally generated by the pullback-unit sections

Let `f : X ⟶ Y` be a morphism of ringed spaces and let `F` be a sheaf of `𝒪_Y`-modules. Every
local section `s` of `F` over an open `V` of `Y` has a canonical image
`η(s) ∈ (f^*F)(f⁻¹V)` under the unit of the adjunction `f^* ⊣ f_*`. This file proves that
these sections **generate `f^*F` locally**: every local section of `f^*F` over an open `W` of
`X` lies, after restriction along the members of a covering of `W`, in the `𝒪_X`-submodule
spanned by the restrictions of the sections `η(s)`.

No hypothesis on `F` is needed — in particular `F` is not assumed of finite type, nor even to
have local generating sections. The argument is formal and uses nothing about the
construction of `f^*`, which matters here because `RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction.modulePullback`
is defined as an abstract left adjoint and has no description of its sections. Let `S ⊆ f^*F`
be the subsheaf of sections *locally* in the span of the `η(s)`. If `g : f^*F ⟶ Z` kills `S`
then it kills every `η(s)`, so its adjoint transpose `η_F ≫ f_*g` vanishes, so `g = 0`; as
the category of sheaves of modules is preadditive this says exactly that the inclusion
`S ⟶ f^*F` is an epimorphism, and an epimorphism of sheaves of modules is locally surjective
(`Stacks.SheafOfModules.EpiMono.imageSieve_mem_of_epi`). Locality of the membership condition
defining `S` then upgrades "locally in `S`" to "in `S`", which is the statement.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.spanSubmodule`: the presheaf submodule of a sheaf of modules spanned
  by a family of local sections, i.e. objectwise the span of all restrictions of members of
  the family.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.spanSieve`: the sieve of arrows along which a section restricts into
  that span.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.localSpan`: the subsheaf of sections which lie locally in the span.
* `Stacks.PullbackUnitGenerators.pullbackUnitSection`: the section `η(s)` of `f^*F` over
  `f⁻¹V` attached to a section `s` of `F` over `V`.
* `Stacks.PullbackUnitGenerators.unitSections`: the family of all restrictions of the sections
  `η(s)`, and `localUnitSpan` for its local span inside `f^*F`.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.transportSection`: the image of a global section of `M` under a
  functor equipped with a unitor, read again as a global section.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Adjunction.epi_of_unit_comp_map_eq_zero`: a morphism into `L.obj M` through which
  the unit of an adjunction factors "against every test morphism" is an epimorphism. This is
  the formal core, stated for an arbitrary adjunction between preadditive categories.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.mem_localSpan_of_epi_ι`: if the inclusion of the local span of a
  family is an epimorphism, then *every* section of the sheaf lies in the local span.
* `Stacks.PullbackUnitGenerators.epi_localSpan_ι`: the inclusion of the local span of the
  pullback-unit sections into `f^*F` is an epimorphism.
* `Stacks.PullbackUnitGenerators.spanSieve_mem`: **every local section of `f^*F` restricts
  into the span of the pullback-unit sections along a covering sieve.**
* `Stacks.PullbackUnitGenerators.exists_mem_span`: the same statement in the pointwise form
  that the topology on a space provides: for every point of `W` there is a smaller open
  containing it on which the section is an `𝒪_X`-combination of restricted pullback-unit
  sections.
* `Stacks.PullbackUnitGenerators.add_mem_unitSections`: the family of pullback-unit sections
  is closed under addition after restriction to a common open, which is what a polarization
  argument on the generators needs. `map_mem_unitSections` is the same for restriction and
  `pullbackUnitSection_naturality`, `pullbackUnitSection_add` and
  `exists_pullbackUnitSection_restrict` are the calculus of these sections.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.map_s_eq_transportSection`: **the sections that Mathlib's
  `SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections.map` produces are, index by index, the transports of the
  original generating sections** — the identification of those sections through
  `SheafOfModules.unitHomEquiv`.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.mem_localSpan_iff`, `spanSieve_arrows` and `mem_sieveOfSection_iff`:
  the unfoldings that make the local span usable, and
  `apply_eq_zero_of_mem_localSpan` the fact that a morphism killing the local span kills
  every section in it.

## Implementation notes

**What is forced.** The subsheaf `S` is `Stacks.SheafOfModules.localImage` of the inclusion of
the span presheaf submodule; that construction and its locality are already in the library, so
nothing about subsheaves is rebuilt here. The one choice is to span by *all* restrictions of
the family rather than by the family itself, which makes the presheaf submodule stable under
restriction with no side condition and costs nothing downstream, since the span is taken
objectwise anyway.

**Universes.** The generic section keeps the site `C : Type u₁` with `Category.{v} C`
arbitrary and puts the sheaf of rings and the modules in one universe `u`; that is inherited
from `Stacks.SheafOfModules.localImage`, which is stated in that form. The ringed-space
section is at a single universe `u`, forced by
`RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction.modulePullback`. Nothing is narrowed relative to the imports.

**No `@[stacks]` attribute.** Local generation of `f^*F` by pullback-unit sections is a step
inside the proofs of Tags 0098 and 01CI, not a numbered statement of its own, and the two Tag
01CI assertions — that `f^*⋀(F) ≅ ⋀(f^*F)` and that the comparison is unique — are not proved
here.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0096](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0096) — pullback of sheaves
  of modules along a morphism of ringed spaces.
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CI) — pullback and the
  tensor, exterior and symmetric algebras of a sheaf of modules; its proof uses local
  generation of `f^*F` by pullback-unit sections.
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01AH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01AH) — epimorphisms of
  sheaves of modules are the locally surjective morphisms.
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory Opposite Limits AlgebraicGeometry TopologicalSpace
open RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction

universe v₁ v₂ u₁ u₂ v u

namespace Stacks.Adjunction

/-! ### The formal core: an adjunction criterion for an epimorphism into `L.obj M` -/

variable {A : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} A] [Preadditive A]
  {B : Type u₂} [Category.{v₂} B] [Preadditive B]
  {L : A ⥤ B} {Rt : B ⥤ A} (adj : L ⊣ Rt) [Rt.Additive]

/-- **An adjunction criterion for an epimorphism into `L.obj M`.** If every morphism out of
`L.obj M` which is killed by `i` has vanishing adjoint transpose, then `i` is an epimorphism.
The hypothesis is what a factorization of the unit through `i` provides, and is verified in
practice by evaluating on sections. -/
theorem epi_of_unit_comp_map_eq_zero {M : A} {S : B} (i : S ⟶ L.obj M)
    (h : ∀ (Z : B) (g : L.obj M ⟶ Z), i ≫ g = 0 → adj.unit.app M ≫ Rt.map g = 0) :
    Epi i := by
  rw [Preadditive.epi_iff_cancel_zero]
  intro Z g hg
  refine (adj.homEquiv M Z).injective ?_
  rw [Adjunction.homEquiv_unit, Adjunction.homEquiv_unit, Functor.map_zero, comp_zero]
  exact h Z g hg

end Stacks.Adjunction

namespace Stacks.SheafOfModules

/-! ### The submodule spanned by a family of local sections -/

variable {C : Type u₁} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{u}}

/-- The presheaf submodule of a sheaf of modules `N` spanned by a family `T` of local
sections: over an object `X`, the span of all restrictions to `X` of members of `T`. Taking
restrictions into the spanning set is what makes the family of spans stable under
restriction. -/
noncomputable def spanSubmodule (N : SheafOfModules.{u} R)
    (T : ∀ X : Cᵒᵖ, Set (N.val.obj X)) : PresheafOfModules.Submodule N.val where
  obj X := Submodule.span (R.obj.obj X)
    {y | ∃ (Z : Cᵒᵖ) (g : Z ⟶ X) (z : N.val.obj Z), z ∈ T Z ∧ N.val.map g z = y}
  map {X Y} h := by
    rw [Submodule.span_le]
    rintro y ⟨Z, g, z, hz, rfl⟩
    exact Submodule.subset_span ⟨Z, g ≫ h, z, hz, by rw [N.val.map_comp]; rfl⟩

variable {N : SheafOfModules.{u} R} {T : ∀ X : Cᵒᵖ, Set (N.val.obj X)}

/-- A member of the family lies in the span. -/
theorem mem_spanSubmodule {X : Cᵒᵖ} {x : N.val.obj X} (hx : x ∈ T X) :
    x ∈ (spanSubmodule N T).obj X :=
  Submodule.subset_span ⟨X, 𝟙 X, x, hx, by rw [N.val.map_id]; rfl⟩

/-- A restriction of a member of the family lies in the span. -/
theorem map_mem_spanSubmodule {X Z : Cᵒᵖ} (g : Z ⟶ X) {z : N.val.obj Z} (hz : z ∈ T Z) :
    N.val.map g z ∈ (spanSubmodule N T).obj X :=
  Submodule.subset_span ⟨Z, g, z, hz, rfl⟩

/-- The sieve of arrows along which a section restricts into the span of a family of local
sections. -/
def spanSieve (N : SheafOfModules.{u} R) (T : ∀ X : Cᵒᵖ, Set (N.val.obj X)) {X : Cᵒᵖ}
    (x : N.val.obj X) : Sieve X.unop where
  arrows W i := N.val.map i.op x ∈ (spanSubmodule N T).obj (op W)
  downward_closed := by
    intro W W' i hi j
    have := (spanSubmodule N T).map_mem j.op hi
    rwa [← PresheafOfModules.map_comp_apply, ← op_comp] at this

/-- Membership in the span sieve is restriction into the span, by definition. -/
theorem spanSieve_arrows {X : Cᵒᵖ} (x : N.val.obj X) {W : C} (i : W ⟶ X.unop) :
    (spanSieve N T x).arrows i ↔ N.val.map i.op x ∈ (spanSubmodule N T).obj (op W) :=
  Iff.rfl

/-- The subsheaf of sections which lie *locally* in the span of a family of local sections. -/
noncomputable def localSpan (N : SheafOfModules.{u} R)
    (T : ∀ X : Cᵒᵖ, Set (N.val.obj X)) : N.Submodule :=
  localImage (spanSubmodule N T).ι

/-- An element of a subobject, read in the ambient module, lies in the subobject's carrier. -/
private theorem mem_of_val_eq {P : N.val.Submodule} {X : Cᵒᵖ} {y : N.val.obj X}
    (t : P.obj X) (h : Subtype.val t = y) : y ∈ P.obj X :=
  h ▸ t.2

/-- Membership in the local span is exactly the covering of the span sieve. -/
theorem mem_localSpan_iff {X : Cᵒᵖ} (x : N.val.obj X) :
    x ∈ (localSpan N T).obj X ↔ spanSieve N T x ∈ J X.unop := by
  refine ⟨fun hx => J.superset_covering ?_ hx, fun hx => J.superset_covering ?_ hx⟩
  · rintro W i ⟨t, ht⟩
    exact mem_of_val_eq t ht
  · intro W i hi
    exact ⟨⟨N.val.map i.op x, hi⟩, rfl⟩

/-- A member of the family lies in the local span. -/
theorem mem_localSpan {X : Cᵒᵖ} {x : N.val.obj X} (hx : x ∈ T X) :
    x ∈ (localSpan N T).obj X :=
  (mem_localSpan_iff x).2 (J.superset_covering (fun _ i _ =>
    map_mem_spanSubmodule (T := T) i.op hx) (J.top_mem _))

/-- Membership in the sieve of a section for the local span is restriction into the local
span, by definition. -/
theorem mem_sieveOfSection_iff {X : Cᵒᵖ} (x : N.val.obj X) {W : C} (i : W ⟶ X.unop) :
    ((localSpan N T).toSubfunctor.sieveOfSection x).arrows i ↔
      N.val.map i.op x ∈ (localSpan N T).obj (op W) :=
  Iff.rfl

/-- A morphism killing the local span kills every section lying in it. -/
theorem apply_eq_zero_of_mem_localSpan {Z : SheafOfModules.{u} R}
    (g : N ⟶ Z) (hg : (localSpan N T).ι ≫ g = 0) {X : Cᵒᵖ} {x : N.val.obj X}
    (hx : x ∈ (localSpan N T).obj X) : g.val.app X x = 0 :=
  congrArg (fun φ : (localSpan N T).toSheafOfModules ⟶ Z => φ.val.app X ⟨x, hx⟩) hg

variable [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]

/-- **If the inclusion of the local span is an epimorphism, every section lies in the local
span.** The membership condition is local, so local surjectivity of the inclusion upgrades to
surjectivity on sections. -/
theorem mem_localSpan_of_epi_ι [Epi (localSpan N T).ι] {X : Cᵒᵖ} (x : N.val.obj X) :
    x ∈ (localSpan N T).obj X := by
  refine (localSpan N T).isSheaf x (J.superset_covering ?_
    (EpiMono.imageSieve_mem_of_epi (localSpan N T).ι x))
  rintro W i ⟨t, ht⟩
  exact mem_of_val_eq t ht

/-- **If the inclusion of the local span of a family is an epimorphism, every section of the
sheaf restricts into the span of that family along a covering sieve.** -/
theorem spanSieve_mem_of_epi_ι [Epi (localSpan N T).ι] {X : Cᵒᵖ} (x : N.val.obj X) :
    spanSieve N T x ∈ J X.unop :=
  (mem_localSpan_iff x).1 (mem_localSpan_of_epi_ι x)

/-! ### The sections produced by `SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections.map` -/

section Transport

variable {C' : Type u₂} [Category.{v₂} C'] {J' : GrothendieckTopology C'}
  {S : Sheaf J' RingCat.{u}} [HasSheafify J' AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [J'.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  (F : _root_.SheafOfModules.{u} R ⥤ _root_.SheafOfModules.{u} S)
  (η : _root_.SheafOfModules.unit S ≅ F.obj (_root_.SheafOfModules.unit R))

/-- The transport of a global section along a functor equipped with a unitor: a global section
of `M` is a morphism out of the unit, and its image under `F`, precomposed with the unitor, is
a morphism out of the unit of the target, i.e. a global section of `F.obj M`. -/
noncomputable def transportSection {M : _root_.SheafOfModules.{u} R} (t : M.sections) :
    (F.obj M).sections :=
  (F.obj M).unitHomEquiv (η.hom ≫ F.map (M.unitHomEquiv.symm t))

/-- **The generating sections that `SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections.map` produces are the
transports of the original ones.** This is the identification of its index-wise sections,
through `SheafOfModules.unitHomEquiv`, with the images of the generating sections. -/
theorem map_s_eq_transportSection {M : _root_.SheafOfModules.{u} R}
    (G : M.GeneratingSections) [Limits.PreservesColimitsOfSize.{u, u} F] (i : G.I) :
    (G.map F η).s i = transportSection F η (G.s i) := by
  have hπ : M.freeHomEquiv G.π i = G.s i :=
    congrFun (M.freeHomEquiv.apply_symm_apply G.s) i
  have hs : M.unitHomEquiv.symm (G.s i) = _root_.SheafOfModules.ιFree i ≫ G.π := by
    rw [← hπ]
    exact _root_.SheafOfModules.unitHomEquiv_symm_freeHomEquiv_apply G.π i
  have key : _root_.SheafOfModules.ιFree i ≫ G.mapFreeHom F η =
      η.hom ≫ F.map (M.unitHomEquiv.symm (G.s i)) := by
    rw [hs]
    simp only [_root_.SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections.mapFreeHom]
    rw [← Category.assoc, _root_.SheafOfModules.ιFree_mapFreeIso_hom, Category.assoc,
      ← CategoryTheory.Functor.map_comp]
  exact congrArg (F.obj M).unitHomEquiv key

end Transport

end Stacks.SheafOfModules

namespace Stacks.PullbackUnitGenerators

/-! ### The pullback-unit sections of `f^*F` -/

open Stacks.SheafOfModules

variable {X Y : RingedSpace.{u, u}} (f : X ⟶ Y) (F : SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing Y))

/-- The section `η(s)` of `f^*F` over `f⁻¹V` attached to a section `s` of `F` over `V`, by the
unit of the adjunction `f^* ⊣ f_*`. -/
noncomputable def pullbackUnitSection (V : (Opens Y.carrier)ᵒᵖ) (s : F.val.obj V) :
    ((modulePullback f).obj F).val.obj ((opensMap f).op.obj V) :=
  ((modulePullbackPushforwardAdjunction f).unit.app F).val.app V s

/-- The family of all restrictions of pullback-unit sections of `f^*F`. -/
def unitSections (W : (Opens X.carrier)ᵒᵖ) :
    Set (((modulePullback f).obj F).val.obj W) :=
  {x | ∃ (V : (Opens Y.carrier)ᵒᵖ) (g : (opensMap f).op.obj V ⟶ W) (s : F.val.obj V),
    ((modulePullback f).obj F).val.map g (pullbackUnitSection f F V s) = x}

/-- A pullback-unit section belongs to the family. -/
theorem pullbackUnitSection_mem_unitSections (V : (Opens Y.carrier)ᵒᵖ) (s : F.val.obj V) :
    pullbackUnitSection f F V s ∈ unitSections f F ((opensMap f).op.obj V) :=
  ⟨V, 𝟙 _, s, by rw [((modulePullback f).obj F).val.map_id]; rfl⟩

/-- Restriction in a pushforward is restriction along the inverse image of the open. -/
theorem modulePushforward_val_map_apply (N : SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing X))
    {V V' : (Opens Y.carrier)ᵒᵖ} (g : V ⟶ V') (x : ((modulePushforward f).obj N).val.obj V) :
    ((modulePushforward f).obj N).val.map g x = N.val.map ((opensMap f).op.map g) x :=
  rfl

/-- The pullback-unit section of a restricted section is the restriction of the pullback-unit
section: this is naturality of the unit of `f^* ⊣ f_*`. -/
theorem pullbackUnitSection_naturality {V V' : (Opens Y.carrier)ᵒᵖ} (g : V ⟶ V')
    (s : F.val.obj V) :
    pullbackUnitSection f F V' (F.val.map g s) =
      ((modulePullback f).obj F).val.map ((opensMap f).op.map g) (pullbackUnitSection f F V s) :=
  have h : ((modulePullback f ⋙ modulePushforward f).obj F).val.map g
        (((modulePullbackPushforwardAdjunction f).unit.app F).val.app V s) =
      ((modulePullback f).obj F).val.map ((opensMap f).op.map g)
        (pullbackUnitSection f F V s) := rfl
  (PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply
    ((modulePullbackPushforwardAdjunction f).unit.app F).val g s).trans h

/-- The pullback-unit section of a sum is the sum of the pullback-unit sections. -/
theorem pullbackUnitSection_add (V : (Opens Y.carrier)ᵒᵖ) (s s' : F.val.obj V) :
    pullbackUnitSection f F V (s + s') =
      pullbackUnitSection f F V s + pullbackUnitSection f F V s' :=
  map_add _ s s'

/-- A restriction of a member of the family is a member of the family. -/
theorem map_mem_unitSections {W W' : (Opens X.carrier)ᵒᵖ} (i : W ⟶ W')
    {x : ((modulePullback f).obj F).val.obj W} (hx : x ∈ unitSections f F W) :
    ((modulePullback f).obj F).val.map i x ∈ unitSections f F W' := by
  obtain ⟨V, g, s, rfl⟩ := hx
  exact ⟨V, g ≫ i, s, by rw [((modulePullback f).obj F).val.map_comp]; rfl⟩

/-- A pullback-unit section restricted along an inverse image is again a pullback-unit
section, of the restricted section. Stated as an existence so that the witness arrives as a
binder at the `F.val.obj` spelling of its type, which is what makes sums of such sections
elaborate. -/
theorem exists_pullbackUnitSection_restrict {V V₀ : (Opens Y.carrier)ᵒᵖ} (h : V ⟶ V₀)
    (s : F.val.obj V) :
    ∃ s₀ : F.val.obj V₀, pullbackUnitSection f F V₀ s₀ =
      ((modulePullback f).obj F).val.map ((opensMap f).op.map h)
        (pullbackUnitSection f F V s) :=
  ⟨F.val.map h s, pullbackUnitSection_naturality f F h s⟩

/-- **The family of pullback-unit sections is closed under addition.** Two members over the
same open come from sections of `F` over opens `V` and `V'`; both restrict to `V ⊓ V'`, where
additivity of the unit of `f^* ⊣ f_*` exhibits the sum as another pullback-unit section. This
is the fact a polarization argument on the generators needs. -/
theorem add_mem_unitSections {W : (Opens X.carrier)ᵒᵖ}
    {x y : ((modulePullback f).obj F).val.obj W} (hx : x ∈ unitSections f F W)
    (hy : y ∈ unitSections f F W) : x + y ∈ unitSections f F W := by
  obtain ⟨V, g, s, rfl⟩ := hx
  obtain ⟨V', g', s', rfl⟩ := hy
  have hle : W.unop ≤ (opensMap f).obj (V.unop ⊓ V'.unop) :=
    fun p hp => ⟨leOfHom g.unop hp, leOfHom g'.unop hp⟩
  obtain ⟨s₀, hs₀⟩ := exists_pullbackUnitSection_restrict f F (V := V)
    (V₀ := op (V.unop ⊓ V'.unop)) (homOfLE inf_le_left).op s
  obtain ⟨s₁, hs₁⟩ := exists_pullbackUnitSection_restrict f F (V := V')
    (V₀ := op (V.unop ⊓ V'.unop)) (homOfLE inf_le_right).op s'
  have hg : g = (opensMap f).op.map (homOfLE (inf_le_left (a := V.unop) (b := V'.unop))).op ≫
      (homOfLE hle).op := Subsingleton.elim _ _
  have hg' : g' = (opensMap f).op.map (homOfLE (inf_le_right (a := V.unop) (b := V'.unop))).op ≫
      (homOfLE hle).op := Subsingleton.elim _ _
  refine ⟨op (V.unop ⊓ V'.unop), (homOfLE hle).op, s₀ + s₁, ?_⟩
  rw [pullbackUnitSection_add, map_add, hs₀, hs₁, ← PresheafOfModules.map_comp_apply,
    ← PresheafOfModules.map_comp_apply, hg, hg']
  rfl

/-- The local span of the pullback-unit sections inside `f^*F`. -/
noncomputable abbrev localUnitSpan : ((modulePullback f).obj F).Submodule :=
  localSpan ((modulePullback f).obj F) (unitSections f F)

/-- The adjoint transpose of a morphism out of `f^*F` which kills the local span of the
pullback-unit sections vanishes. -/
theorem unit_comp_map_eq_zero (Z : SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing X))
    (g : (modulePullback f).obj F ⟶ Z) (hg : (localUnitSpan f F).ι ≫ g = 0) :
    (modulePullbackPushforwardAdjunction f).unit.app F ≫ (modulePushforward f).map g = 0 := by
  ext V s
  exact apply_eq_zero_of_mem_localSpan g hg
    (mem_localSpan (pullbackUnitSection_mem_unitSections f F V s))

/-- **The inclusion of the local span of the pullback-unit sections into `f^*F` is an
epimorphism.** -/
theorem epi_localSpan_ι : Epi (localUnitSpan f F).ι :=
  Stacks.Adjunction.epi_of_unit_comp_map_eq_zero (modulePullbackPushforwardAdjunction f) _
    (unit_comp_map_eq_zero f F)

/-- **Every local section of `f^*F` lies locally in the span of the pullback-unit
sections.** -/
theorem mem_localUnitSpan (W : (Opens X.carrier)ᵒᵖ)
    (x : ((modulePullback f).obj F).val.obj W) : x ∈ (localUnitSpan f F).obj W :=
  let := epi_localSpan_ι f F
  mem_localSpan_of_epi_ι x

/-- **A pullback of sheaves of modules is locally generated by the pullback-unit sections:**
every local section of `f^*F` over `W` restricts, along the arrows of a covering sieve of `W`,
into the `𝒪_X`-submodule spanned by the restrictions of the sections `η(s)`. -/
theorem spanSieve_mem (W : (Opens X.carrier)ᵒᵖ)
    (x : ((modulePullback f).obj F).val.obj W) :
    spanSieve ((modulePullback f).obj F) (unitSections f F) x ∈
      Opens.grothendieckTopology X.carrier W.unop :=
  let := epi_localSpan_ι f F
  spanSieve_mem_of_epi_ι x

/-- The pointwise form of local generation: every point of `W` has an open neighbourhood
inside `W` on which the section is an `𝒪_X`-linear combination of restricted pullback-unit
sections. -/
theorem exists_mem_span (W : (Opens X.carrier)ᵒᵖ)
    (x : ((modulePullback f).obj F).val.obj W) (p : X.carrier) (hp : p ∈ W.unop) :
    ∃ (W' : Opens X.carrier) (i : W' ⟶ W.unop), p ∈ W' ∧
      ((modulePullback f).obj F).val.map i.op x ∈
        (spanSubmodule ((modulePullback f).obj F) (unitSections f F)).obj (op W') := by
  obtain ⟨W', i, hi, hpW'⟩ := spanSieve_mem f F W x p hp
  exact ⟨W', i, hpW', hi⟩

end Stacks.PullbackUnitGenerators

end
